### Case: seed-known-pattern — generate labelled traffic to query against.
###
### Analytics is capture-then-query. Without traffic there is nothing to verify, and
### without KNOWN traffic there is nothing to verify against. ../gateway/verify.sh
### does all of this and prints the exact counts and window timestamps; these are the
### individual requests it makes, if you want to run them by hand.
###
### 1. Successes on the collection route (default 12x)
GET {{GATEWAY}}/orders
authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
accept: application/json

###
### 2. The TEMPLATED item route (default 2x). These must aggregate under
###    /orders/{orderId} in a per-route breakdown — NOT as a row per identifier.
###    This is the path-templating case, and it is the one that matters most.
GET {{GATEWAY}}/orders/verify-probe-001
authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
accept: application/json

###
### 3. Deliberate auth failures (default 3x), with an obviously-labelled forged token.
###    These have NO app to attribute to — identity never resolved — so expect them in
###    an unidentified bucket. That is correct behaviour, not a gap.
GET {{GATEWAY}}/orders
authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJwcm9iZSJ9.deliberate-verify-probe-failure
accept: application/json

###
### 4. The slow route, for the latency-profile-separation case. Call it a few times so
###    its distribution is visibly different from the fast reads above.
POST {{GATEWAY}}/orders/report
authorization: Bearer {{ACCESS_TOKEN}}
content-type: application/json

{"from":"2026-01-01","to":"2026-01-31"}
